WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:07.540
Interviewer: What do you make of the European premier in Berlin? How does it look?

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:10.780
Martin: Well I think it looks fantastic. I love the big dragon, I love those Christmas lights,

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:15.540
Martin:  I love this *enormous* carpet, and I've always loved Berlin, so yeah, I'm happy.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.260
Interviewer: And how's it to meet all your fellow cast members again?

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.080
Martin: Well, I've not really done it yet, because every time I go near someone, someone whisks me away.

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:25.840
Martin: I'm just waving at them from across the room, at the moment.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.500
Martin: But we'll catch up in a minute.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:31.060
Interviewer: What does it mean actually meeting the fans for you? How special is that?

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:37.800
Martin: It's very special. There are some very special people out there, and uh, they've been queueing up for a very long time.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:39.940
Martin: Which we're very appreciative of, yeah.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:45.560
Interviewer: Did having worked with Benedict Cumberbatch on Sherlock help you for this movie to work together again,

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.700
Interviewer: because you didn't really share a room together.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:54.060
Martin: No, we didn't. Uh, I mean, it didn't hurt,  it was, it was nice, but it didn't really help.  In a way.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:55.760
Martin:  I mean, it didn't hurt it, but it didn't help,

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:57.920
Martin: because I'm just imagining everything anyways, do you know what I mean?

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:05.900
Martin: So, it would have been perfect to do it with Ben, but we weren't able to, so you just gotta use your imagination.

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:08.340
Interviewer: Could you second-guess his performance maybe in a way?

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:12.560
Martin: No. Not really, no. No, I mean, no, because he's good!

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:14.660
Martin: So you know, so you can't expect too much.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:17.360
Martin: Or you can't guess too much because he's going to surprise you.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:19.980
Interviewer: Are you excited about Sherlock coming out?

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:22.920
Martin: No, I hate Sherlock. No, I can't stand it (laughs).

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:27.700
Interviewer: Because I was wondering, what can fans expect from the new season of Sherlock?  They're really excited I guess.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:28.400
Martin: Are they?

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:29.440
Interviewer: They are, yeah.

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:31.040
Martin: Who's excited about Sherlock?

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:33.200
Martin: Do people watch it?

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:34.600
Interviewer: They do, yes!

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:38.340
Martin: No, of course I'm excited about it.  I think it's going to be great.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:42.320
Martin: I've seen all three of them now. I think they're... they're fantastic!

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:46.720
Martin: They're fantastic. They were brilliant scripts, Ben does a great job again,

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:53.280
Martin: It's a thoroughly enjoyable job. It's one of my favorite jobs I've ever done. Or ever will do, yeah, we love doing it, yeah.

